{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n\nOn 2026-11-10 ~19:55 PST `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3344 --revision <sha>` reportedly exited 1, yet change 3344 is MERGED (merge commit 9f8b2af21c8 on origin/main). The script's stderr was not captured.\n\n## Root-cause evidence (read-only, Gerrit `httpd_log` on i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\nThat invocation made exactly 3 requests, all `Python-urllib/3.12` from the same client, all HTTP 200:\n- 03:55:04.357Z `GET /a/changes/3344?o=CURRENT_REVISION&o=DETAILED_LABELS&o=SUBMITTABLE` 200\n- 03:55:04.653Z `POST /a/changes/3344/hashtags` 200\n- 03:55:05.109Z `POST /a/changes/3344/revisions/7a3baab7a2c6.../submit` 200 (Gerrit rebased and merged)\n\nSo none of the script's HTTP paths failed, and no request timed out. On the success path the script returns 0, so the reported exit 1 is not attributable to a Gerrit response; it most likely came from the calling shell, which no evidence recovers. The script still has a real defect the ticket names: any exception after the vote check (a non-409 `HTTPError`, a `URLError`/timeout, or an unparseable body from the hashtag or submit request) escapes as a traceback with exit 1, even when Gerrit has already merged the change. This plan fixes that class for every such path.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py`:\n1. The session-hashtag POST becomes best-effort: any `HTTPError`, `URLError`, `OSError` or `ValueError` prints a warning naming the error and continues to the submit (a missing ownership tag must not block or misreport a submit).\n2. The submit POST catches `HTTPError` (non-409), `URLError`, `OSError` (timeouts) and `ValueError` (unparseable body). It then re-reads the change with all revisions: if `status` is `MERGED` and the requested revision is one of the change's revisions, it prints `submitted: change <n> merged (revision <sha>)` and returns 0; otherwise it prints the original error and Gerrit's response body (for an `HTTPError`) and returns 1. A failure of that re-read is reported with the original error and returns 1. The 409 path is unchanged (exit 2).\n3. The module docstring's exit-code table documents exit 1 as \"the submit failed and the change is not merged\" and drops \"re-raises\".\nNo new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests with a stubbed `_request` (same style as the existing tests):\n- submit raises non-409 `HTTPError` (502) but the re-read shows MERGED with the revision → exit 0, prints \"merged\";\n- submit raises `URLError` (timeout) but MERGED → exit 0;\n- submit returns an unparseable body (`ValueError`) but MERGED → exit 0;\n- submit raises 502 and the re-read shows NEW → exit 1, stderr has Gerrit's body;\n- submit raises `URLError` and the re-read itself fails → exit 1 naming both;\n- hashtag POST raises 500 → warning on stderr, submit still runs, exit 0;\n- the existing 409 tests pass unchanged; the existing `test_safe_submit_reraises_non_409_submit_http_error` is replaced by the not-merged exit-1 test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] The 3344 incident's request trail is recorded on this ticket (3 requests, all 200), showing the script's own HTTP calls did not fail.\n  provenance: environment=production Gerrit host i-00880b2c7f13527c5 httpd_log via SSM; principal=frontier AWS profile; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read-only grep of the request log\n- [x] Every exception path after the vote check (hashtag POST, submit POST: non-409 HTTPError, URLError/timeout, unparseable body) has a unit test.\n- [x] A submit that raises after Gerrit merged the requested revision exits 0 and prints that it merged.\n- [x] A submit that fails without merging exits 1 and prints Gerrit's response body.\n- [x] The 409 path's behaviour and tests are unchanged.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-milksnake worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794469455707669001,"uuid":"bf4ae598-c9b8-4f9b-a34c-580c6a6d9ed0"}